% The London Underground Emergency Notice, as beliefs, in Logical English.
%
%     Emergencies
%     Press the alarm signal button to alert the driver.
%     The driver will stop if any part of the train is in a station.
%     If not, the train will continue to the next station,
%     where help can more easily be given.
%     There is a 50 pound penalty for improper use.
%
% After R. Kowalski, Computational Logic and Human Thinking, chapter 1.

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    *a person* presses the alarm signal button of *a train*.
    the driver of *a train* is alerted.
    *a part* of *a train* is in *a station*.
    *a train* stops in *a station*.
    *a train* continues to the next station.
    *a person* is liable to a penalty of *an amount*.
    *a person* uses the alarm signal button improperly; unknown.

the knowledge base emergency notice includes:

rule sentence_1 with provenance the Emergency Notice, confer "Press the alarm signal button to alert the driver":
the driver of a train is alerted
    if a person presses the alarm signal button of the train.

rule sentence_2 with provenance the Emergency Notice, confer "The driver will stop if any part of the train is in a station":
a train stops in a station
    if the driver of the train is alerted
    and a part of the train is in the station.

rule sentence_3 with provenance the Emergency Notice, confer "If not, the train will continue to the next station":
a train continues to the next station
    if the driver of the train is alerted
    and it is not the case that
        a part of the train is in a station.

rule sentence_4 with provenance the Emergency Notice, confer "There is a 50 pound penalty for improper use":
a person is liable to a penalty of 50
    if the person presses the alarm signal button of a train
    and the person uses the alarm signal button improperly.

scenario in a station is:
    alice presses the alarm signal button of the 8:15.
    the last carriage of the 8:15 is in Victoria.
    stops expects answers ["the 8:15 stops in Victoria"].
    continues expects answers [].

scenario between stations is:
    alice presses the alarm signal button of the 8:15.
    stops expects answers [].
    continues expects answers ["the 8:15 continues to the next station"].
    penalty expects answers ["alice is liable to a penalty of 50"]
        and unknowns ["alice uses the alarm signal button improperly"].

query stops is:
    which train stops in which station.

query continues is:
    which train continues to the next station.

query penalty is:
    which person is liable to a penalty of which amount.
